<title>LEBANON: Lebanese bank sector grew strongly in '96 - report.</title>
<headline>Lebanese bank sector grew strongly in '96 - report.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's banking sector grew substantially in 1996 in terms of assets, deposits and loans, a Lebanese business magazine reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The weekly Al-Iktissad Wal-Aamal issued a preliminary ranking of the country's top 18 banks -- based on their unaudited 1996 results.</p>
<p>The Paris-based magazine said total assets of these leading banks rose 35 percent to $20.3 billion at the end of 1996 from $15 billion a year earlier. Total deposits also jumped by 40 percent reaching $17.6 billion against $12.5 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>Loans to the private sector increased by 35 percent to $6.3 billion in 1996 from $4.6 billion a year earlier, the magazine said.</p>
<p>&quot;The preliminary unaudited results of Lebanon's top 18 banks give important indicators to the big growth achieved by the banking sector in Lebanon,&quot; it added.</p>
